## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your understanding of end-to-end performance testing for complex streaming architectures under bursty conditions, including backpressure behavior and cross-region autoscaling.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end latency distribution and tail latency (p99, p999) in multi-stage pipelines
- Backpressure propagation and saturation points across Kafka, Flink, feature store, and inference services
- Regional autoscaling, circuit breakers, and traffic shaping strategies
- Realistic workload modeling with appropriate traffic patterns and mix

## Code Example
```java
// Example: Backpressure simulation using Kafka Streams
public class BackpressureTest {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Properties props = new Properties();
        props.put("application.id", "latency-test");
        props.put("num.stream.threads", 4);

        // Configure max poll records to control backpressure
        props.put("max.poll.records", 100);
        props.put("max.poll.interval.ms", 300000);

        // Set producer buffering for burst handling
        props.put("buffer.memory", 67108864);
        props.put("batch.size", 16384);

        KafkaStreams streams = new KafkaStreams(builder.build(), props);
        streams.start();

        // Monitor backpressure metrics
        streams.metrics().forEach((name, metric) -> {
            if (name.contains("poll-latency")) {
                System.out.println(name + ": " + metric.metricValue());
            }
        });
    }
}
```

